Package: dynarules
Title: Association and Sequential Rule Mining for Temporal Event Data
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R:
    person("Mohammed", "Saqr", email = "ueflaunit@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Mines association rules and order-aware sequential rules from
    temporal event data -- coded behaviors, learning traces, and interaction
    logs -- using a clean-room, base-R implementation of level-wise Apriori
    and generalized sequential pattern mining. Transactions are constructed
    from an explicit event-log grammar (actor, action, time, session, window)
    rather than assumed, so the unit of analysis is a modeling decision, not
    an input format. Every mined rule set supports post-hoc filtering through
    tidy verbs, conversion to a plottable network object, bootstrap stability
    assessment, and permutation-based significance testing (including an
    order-shuffling null that isolates the temporal component of sequential
    rules).
